# 🟣 Refactoring

These are extremely valuable as you become a better engineer.

| Verb          | Meaning                                                           | Example                                          |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `Refactor`    | Change internal structure without intentionally changing behavior | `Refactor cart operations into helper functions` |
| `Extract`     | Move logic into a separate function/module                        | `Extract post lookup into helper`                |
| `Consolidate` | Combine duplicated or scattered logic                             | `Consolidate validation logic`                   |
| `Simplify`    | Make code easier or less complicated                              | `Simplify checkout logic`                        |
| `Separate`    | Split responsibilities                                            | `Separate route and database logic`              |
| `Encapsulate` | Hide implementation behind a function/module/class                | `Encapsulate cart calculations`                  |
| `Decompose`   | Break a large piece into smaller pieces                           | `Decompose checkout workflow`                    |
| `Modularize`  | Organize code into independent modules                            | `Modularize post management`                     |
| `Reorganize`  | Change code organization                                          | `Reorganize Express routes`                      |
| `Decouple`    | Reduce unnecessary dependencies between components                | `Decouple cart and product logic`                |

These become particularly useful once you're doing serious code reviews.

---

# 🟠 Removing Things

| Verb        | Meaning                                         | Example                        |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| `Remove`    | Delete unnecessary code/functionality           | `Remove duplicate validation`  |
| `Delete`    | Permanently remove something                    | `Delete unused routes`         |
| `Drop`      | Remove a feature/dependency/table/etc.          | `Drop unused database column`  |
| `Clean`     | Remove clutter or unnecessary files/code        | `Clean unused imports`         |
| `Prune`     | Remove unnecessary pieces                       | `Prune obsolete configuration` |
| `Deprecate` | Mark something as no longer recommended for use | `Deprecate legacy API route`   |

**Don't use `Delete` and `Remove` randomly.**

For example:

> `Remove unused function`

sounds natural.

> `Delete user authentication`

sounds like you're intentionally destroying a feature.

