# 🟤 Improving Code Quality

| Verb          | Meaning                                                    | Example                       |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `Clean`       | Remove unnecessary complexity/clutter                      | `Clean cart validation logic` |
| `Simplify`    | Reduce complexity                                          | `Simplify product lookup`     |
| `Optimize`    | Improve performance/resource usage                         | `Optimize product search`     |
| `Improve`     | General quality improvement                                | `Improve error handling`      |
| `Harden`      | Make software more resistant to failures/security problems | `Harden authentication flow`  |
| `Strengthen`  | Improve robustness                                         | `Strengthen input validation` |
| `Standardize` | Make things follow a consistent pattern                    | `Standardize API responses`   |
| `Normalize`   | Put data/structure into a consistent form                  | `Normalize product data`      |

Be careful with **optimize**.

Don't use:

> `Optimize code`

just because you changed code.

Use it when you actually improved performance or resource usage.

